From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:29:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: remove 5 GHz channels 68 and 96

The mt7996 pre-calibration and testmode patch adds channels 68-96
to the shared mt76_channels_5ghz table. Drop 68 and 96 again: they
are unusable in every shipped regulatory domain. The remaining
72-92 block stays exposed but is inert and carries no DPD slots.

Also trim the mt7996 dpd_5g_skip_ch_list from 8 to 6 entries and
MT76_CHANNELS_5GHZ_SIZE from 36 to 34 so BW20 5G DPD keeps its 28
slots (channels 36-64 and 100-177); with the skip list left at 8
entries the factory calibration mis-mapped for channels >= 100 and
the blob was under-read.

The channel table hunk is generic mac80211.c code and affects all
mt76 drivers, not only mt7996.

Fixes: OWRT-9554

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mac80211.c      |    2 --
 mt7996/eeprom.c |    6 ++----
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -34,14 +34,12 @@ static const struct ieee80211_channel mt
 	CHAN5G(60, 5300),
 	CHAN5G(64, 5320),
 
-	CHAN5G(68, 5340),
 	CHAN5G(72, 5360),
 	CHAN5G(76, 5380),
 	CHAN5G(80, 5400),
 	CHAN5G(84, 5420),
 	CHAN5G(88, 5440),
 	CHAN5G(92, 5460),
-	CHAN5G(96, 5480),
 
 	CHAN5G(100, 5500),
 	CHAN5G(104, 5520),
--- a/mt7996/eeprom.c
+++ b/mt7996/eeprom.c
@@ -14,14 +14,12 @@ const struct ieee80211_channel dpd_2g_ch
 };
 
 const struct ieee80211_channel dpd_5g_skip_ch_list[] = {
-	CHAN5G(68, 5340),
 	CHAN5G(72, 5360),
 	CHAN5G(76, 5380),
 	CHAN5G(80, 5400),
 	CHAN5G(84, 5420),
 	CHAN5G(88, 5440),
-	CHAN5G(92, 5460),
-	CHAN5G(96, 5480)
+	CHAN5G(92, 5460)
 };
 
 const struct ieee80211_channel dpd_5g_ch_list_bw80[] = {
@@ -406,7 +404,7 @@ int mt7996_eeprom_parse_hw_cap(struct mt
 
 static void mt7996_eeprom_init_precal(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 {
-#define MT76_CHANNELS_5GHZ_SIZE		36	/* ARRAY_SIZE(mt76_channels_5ghz) */
+#define MT76_CHANNELS_5GHZ_SIZE		34	/* ARRAY_SIZE(mt76_channels_5ghz) */
 #define MT76_CHANNELS_6GHZ_SIZE		59	/* ARRAY_SIZE(mt76_channels_6ghz) */
 
 	dev->prek.dpd_ch_num[DPD_CH_NUM_BW20_2G] = ARRAY_SIZE(dpd_2g_ch_list_bw20);
